+# Litware Support
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Go-live | 2027-W11 (contract: `docs/LITWARE_SOW.md`) |
+| Grain / timezone | 20 minutes / Europe/London |
+| Operating hours | 07:00-21:00 local, seven days; `email` contacts arrive 07:00-19:00 |
+| Queues | priority (90/30), standard (80/30), email (80/300); occupancy cap 0.85 |
+| Config | `configs/litware.yaml` (schema 1) |
+| Roster | `data/agents/litware.csv`, 24 agents (6 part-time) |
+| Data | `data/litware/export_<ISO>.csv`, local time stamped with the END of the interval, `utc_offset` per row (see its README) |
+| Scheduler | `weekly` (SOW 2.1-2.6); weekly attainment target 0.95 per queue, hours <= 1.45 x required |
+
+`python -m wfm run --client litware --week <ISO>` writes `schedule.csv`, `eval.json`, `RUNBOOK.md` and `exceptions.md`
+under `out/litware/` (about 12 s, seeded and deterministic). Rules specific to Litware: two agents on `priority` in
+every operating interval (`min_cover`), nobody on `email` before 09:00 (`queue_earliest_start`; the 07:00-09:00 email
+intervals with demand are SOW 2.6 exceptions), PT-only splits, 11 h rest.
+
+What changed and the deviations that predate it: `litware_handover.md` (embedded in `RUNBOOK.md`).
